[1] Difference Between Synchronous and Asynchronous File Operations
(a) Synchronous Operations
1. Execute one task at a time.
2. Block the execution until the file operation is completed.
3. Use methods like readFileSync() and writeFileSync().
4. Simple to use.
5. Not suitable for large or real-time applications.

(b) Asynchronous Operations
1. Do not block program execution.
2. Run in the background.
3. Use methods like readFile() and writeFile().
4. Improve performance.
5.Recommended for real-world applications.

